{
  "version": 4,
  "description": "Per-tenant feature switches (spec C6). A Super Admin turns these on or off for a tenant in Manage Tenant; the list is stored in tenants.enabledFeatures. Groups follow the sidebar sections (shared/catalogue-access.json), and every sidebar item a tenant role can reach has its own switch: either its permission's switch (when no other item shares that permission) or a \"screen:<view>\" switch. For users of that tenant the server removes every switched-off permission, and every permission on the same resource as a switched-off view:X (manage:X and the like), from what their role grants. A feature with a parent is off whenever its parent is off. A \"screen:<view>\" switch turns one sidebar item off: the sidebar hides it and the server refuses the routes the item owns in the manifest, unless the entry is \"hideOnly\" (its routes serve other screens too). A screen with no parent hangs only on the permission its manifest entry names (Overview, Tickets, My Tasks ...). Read by backend/tenant_features.py, components/ManageTenantModal.tsx and utils/permissions.ts. Every screen switch sits in the group of its sidebar section. Every screen is on only when a Super Admin ticks it: a new tenant (sign-up or Add Tenant) starts with Overview only (tenant_features.START_FEATURES), and switching a feature on, or picking a tier, does not switch its screens on. Groups marked \"explicitScreens\" (Security, Compliance) were explicit first; migrations 017 and 018 still read that mark.",
